From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: qcom-wled: track initially disabled OVP IRQ

The imported WLED IRQ balance fix tracks IRQ depth during brightness
changes, but the pre-existing probe path also disables OVP IRQ when the
module starts off. Record that transition so the first brightness
change can re-enable it.

Fixes: 5865d04a7b41 ("backlight: qcom-wled: fix unbalanced enable irq")
Source-Commit: https://github.com/sdm660-mainline/linux/commit/5865d04a7b415e2ab0330089c3d8d34a0d6a9f6f
Scope: Shared-driver
Porting notes: Local correction found during 7.3-rc5 migration review; 0014 remains the original source hunk.
---
diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c b/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
@@ -1656,8 +1656,10 @@
 		return rc;
 
 	/* Keep OVP irq disabled until module is enabled */
-	if (!(val & WLED3_CTRL_REG_MOD_EN_MASK))
+	if (!(val & WLED3_CTRL_REG_MOD_EN_MASK)) {
 		disable_irq(wled->ovp_irq);
+		wled->ovp_irq_disabled = true;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
